<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="032" project="email-communication-intelligence-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Job B queue-feed endpoint — ranked exceptions feed for r5 (feed only; r1 builds NO UI, C-3)</title>
    <phase>P3 — Job B record currency</phase>
    <gate>after:030</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds a NEW read endpoint on the shared `Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` family that is the sole feed for r5's Exceptions Queue surface. It composes ranked exceptions (unresolved associations + pending Job B proposals + Suggested/Ambiguous items) and MUST apply the same access posture as the rest of the communication read surface — no over-disclosure. BFF-touching: publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification; code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>A read/feed endpoint composing already-produced data (proposals from 030 + association statuses) into a ranked list; no design judgment beyond ranking + access posture; well-specified.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Extends the shared `Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` family (same file as 031); serialize after 030 and never concurrent with other shared `Services/Communication/` writers. `/conflict-check` before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <dependencies>030</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement the **queue-feed** endpoint (FR-17): a surface-agnostic read endpoint that returns the **ranked exceptions** for a scope (e.g. matter / user / tenant) — the items needing human attention: unresolved / `Suggested` / `Ambiguous` associations plus pending Job B proposals (from 030). **r1 supplies the feed ONLY; r5 builds the Exceptions Queue surface (C-3).** r1 builds no UI.

    Add the route to the EXISTING `Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` communication group (extend the `suggest-associations` family — no new group). The feed contract MUST be consumable by BOTH r5 surfaces (Code Page + SpaarkeAi widget) without a fork (D-10). Rank by attention-worthiness (e.g. RI-confidence / priority / recency — reuse the triage priority + RI-confidence already computed on `sprk_communication`; do NOT invent a second scoring scheme).

    Apply the same access posture as the rest of the communication read surface (caller resolved server-side; no over-disclosure). Read-only — this endpoint mutates nothing.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication domain, authoritative on `Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` reads, the Job B pending-proposal shape (030), the association status model (`Suggested`/`Ambiguous`), the triage priority + RI-confidence fields on `sprk_communication`, ADR-008 (endpoint filters), ADR-019 (ProblemDetails), and the r5 feed coordination contract (C-3, D-10).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A read endpoint on the existing `/api/communications` group returns a ranked exceptions feed for a scope — unresolved/Suggested/Ambiguous associations + pending Job B proposals — in a shape both r5 surfaces render without a fork. Ranking reuses the existing triage priority + RI-confidence (no second scoring scheme). The endpoint applies the communication read access posture (no over-disclosure), carries the ADR-008 filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails, is registered unconditionally, and is read-only. Build clean; unit + seam tests pass; publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      C-3 resolved: r5 builds the Exceptions Queue *surface*; r1 supplies the *feed*. This endpoint is that feed — the ranked list of items a reviewer acts on. It composes what the spine already produced: association outcomes (020/021 — unresolved / `Suggested` / `Ambiguous`) and pending Job B proposals (030). It does NOT re-run triage or re-score; it reads the priority + RI-confidence already on `sprk_communication` (024/025) and the stored proposals (030), then ranks.

      D-10: both r5 surfaces (Code Page + SpaarkeAi widget) consume the same feed — the contract must be dual-use, no fork. The coordination doc pins the feed shape. r1 builds no UI (Success Criterion coordination, not a task).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs (ADD the queue-feed route to the existing `/api/communications` group — no new group)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ (REFERENCE — association status model + the read/query services the feed reuses)</file>
      <file>sprk_communication (Dataverse — triage priority + RI-confidence fields to rank by; association status)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/email-intelligence-r1-coordination.md (r5 feed contract — the dual-use ranked-exceptions shape both r5 surfaces render, C-3 / D-10)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>030 (pending Job B proposals are part of the ranked feed).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-17 / C-3">Scope: expose a surface-agnostic queue-feed returning ranked exceptions (unresolved/Suggested/Ambiguous associations + pending Job B proposals); r1 supplies the FEED only — r5 builds the surface. r1 builds no UI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-10">Scope: the feed contract MUST be consumable by BOTH r5 surfaces (Code Page + SpaarkeAi widget) without a fork; pin the shape to the coordination doc.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-08 / project">Scope: rank by reusing the existing email-specific triage priority + RI-confidence already computed on `sprk_communication`; do NOT invent a second scoring/priority scheme (no Workspace/Portfolio scoring reuse).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / ADR-019">Scope: the route carries the communication authorization endpoint filter + RFC 7807 ProblemDetails on error; caller resolved server-side; register unconditionally (ADR-032/ADR-010); read-only (mutates nothing).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state Placement Justification (extends the `suggest-associations` family; thin minimal-API; no new group); publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB (expected ≈0); no new HIGH CVE; update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §11">Scope: Component Justification — the queue-feed is new only because r5 has no ranked-exceptions read; state the concrete FR-17 failure mode prevented (r5 has no exceptions queue data) with grep evidence that no existing route returns a ranked exceptions feed.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/spec.md</file>
