  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`, the coordination doc (dual-use feed shape), and `DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md`.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `CommunicationEndpoints.cs` (the `suggest-associations` family + auth filter) + the association status model + the triage priority / RI-confidence fields. Grep to confirm no existing ranked-exceptions feed route (§11 evidence).</step>
    <step order="3">Design the dual-use ranked-exceptions DTO (per coordination doc): item ref, kind (unresolved-association / Suggested / Ambiguous / pending-proposal), rank score (from existing priority + RI-confidence), and enough for r5 to render both surfaces. Keep it minimal + fork-free.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the feed: read unresolved/Suggested/Ambiguous association outcomes + pending Job B proposals (030) for the scope; rank by the existing priority + RI-confidence; apply the communication read access posture (caller server-side; no over-disclosure); page deterministically.</step>
    <step order="5">Add the queue-feed route to the existing `/api/communications` group: bind scope + paging, apply the ADR-008 filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails; register unconditionally (ADR-032/ADR-010); read-only.</step>
    <step order="6">Write unit + seam tests: (a) the feed returns ranked exceptions for a scope including a pending proposal + a Suggested/Ambiguous association; (b) ranking reuses the existing priority + RI-confidence (no second scheme); (c) NEGATIVE — an item the caller may not see is absent (no over-disclosure); (d) the DTO is dual-use (one shape, no surface fork). ADR-038 boundary mocks only.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + targeted `dotnet test`; publish-size (report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB) + CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor gates: `code-review` (focus no-over-disclosure, no second scoring scheme, dual-use no-fork, read-only); `adr-check` against ADR-045 + spec FR-17 / D-08 / D-10. Address Critical findings; cite Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` + endpoint family; coordinate with 031 on the same file).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (032 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (feed DTO shape, ranking inputs, access posture) for the r5 handoff.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The `suggest-associations` endpoint family returns per-message association suggestions; there is no route that returns a ranked exceptions queue across a scope, and no store of pending Job B proposals existed before 030.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — this is one additive read route + a composition over already-produced data (association outcomes + 030 proposals), reusing the existing priority + RI-confidence signals + the communication read access posture; no new service, no new scoring scheme.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the queue-feed, r5's Exceptions Queue surface has no data source — the reviewer has no single ranked list of items needing attention (FR-17 fails; Success Criterion coordination with r5 breaks).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Inspect the endpoint family, association status model, triage/RI fields, coordination doc</tool>
    <tool name="grep">Confirm no existing ranked-exceptions feed route (§11); confirm no second scoring scheme introduced</tool>
    <tool name="edit">Add the queue-feed route + feed composition</tool>
    <tool name="bash">Build, unit/seam tests, publish-size, CVE scan</tool>
    <tool name="code-review">FULL-rigor gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="adr-check">FULL-rigor gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">Pre-PR hot-path scan (Step 10)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs (UPDATED — ranked queue-feed route on the existing group; access-posture-applied; unconditional; read-only)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ (UPDATED — ranked-exceptions composition reusing existing priority + RI-confidence)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + tests/integration/seam/ — ranked-feed + reuse-ranking + no-over-disclosure + dual-use-no-fork</output>
    <output type="docs">PR description with §11 Component Justification + bff-extensions Placement Justification + publish-size delta + CVE result; feed DTO handoff note for r5</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The queue-feed returns ranked exceptions for a scope, including pending Job B proposals (030) and Suggested/Ambiguous associations, in a single dual-use DTO both r5 surfaces render without a fork.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Ranking reuses the existing email-specific triage priority + RI-confidence on `sprk_communication`; no second scoring/priority scheme is introduced (grep-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: an item the caller may not see is absent from the feed (no over-disclosure); the caller is resolved server-side.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The endpoint is read-only (mutates nothing), carries the ADR-008 filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails, and is registered unconditionally.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">r1 builds no UI — this task delivers the feed contract only (C-3).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; tests pass; publish-size delta ≈0 vs ~49.63 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    r1 supplies the feed; r5 builds the surface (C-3). The feed must be dual-use (Code Page + widget) without a fork (D-10). Reuse the existing priority + RI-confidence for ranking — do not invent a second scheme (D-08). Coordinate the DTO shape with the r5 coordination doc. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shares `CommunicationEndpoints.cs` with 031).
  </notes>

